            <div xml:id="d876">

                <pb facs="0883" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg625"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2052</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1915-12-09T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1915-12-06T00:00:00+00:00">undated</date> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received December 9, 1915</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi>
                </p>
                <p>With a view to meeting American complaints Sir Edward Grey is ready to set up a
                    small unofficial committee of persons of experience who shall examine any
                    specific case in which an allegation is made of unnecessary delay in dealing
                    with ships and cargoes from the United States. This committee would also suggest
                    any improvements in the machinery for the purpose of preventing such delays in
                    other cases.</p>
            </div>
